Hi, Randy,

On Mon, Nov 18, 2024 at 8:32=E2=80=AFPM Turner, Randy
<Randy.Turner=3D40landisgyr.com@dmarc.ietf.org> wrote:
> In our tests of RFC 7925 recommendations/requirements, the mandate for th=
e CCM_8 AES algorithms seems to be outdated =E2=80=93 from our tests, both =
Microsoft and OpenSSL have deprecated or removed support for the CCM_8 algo=
rithms =E2=80=93 we have seen this when CCM_8 algorithms are offered by TLS=
 clients to TLS servers running Microsoft=E2=80=99s crypto provider (Window=
s server 2019) or a server linked to the latest OpenSSL 3 release
>
> Is there a recommended replacement or =E2=80=9Cbis=E2=80=9D work proceedi=
ng with new recommendations ?

The place is UTA [1] -- more precisely, Section 18 of
I-D.ietf-uta-tls13-iot-profile [2].

(I am not sure it is possible to fully deprecate CCM_8 at this time
because of constrained-to-constrained scenarios. However, we have
started recommending its non-truncated sibling alongside GCM.)

[1] https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/uta/
[2] https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-uta-tls13-iot-profile-11.htm=
l#section-18

--=20
Thomas

